WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.629
Now we will run our first code

00:00:01.642 --> 00:00:05.026
example for this module This cell imports

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:08.579
three tools from Python's standard library The

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:11.868
first line imports the math module The

00:00:11.895 --> 00:00:15.329
second line imports the random module The

00:00:15.355 --> 00:00:17.368
third line imports only the date class

00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:20.421
from the datetime module Notice that the

00:00:20.447 --> 00:00:22.974
third import uses a slightly different style

00:00:23.908 --> 00:00:26.461
Instead of importing the entire datetime module

00:00:26.711 --> 00:00:29.658
we say from datetime import date This

00:00:29.671 --> 00:00:31.526
gives us direct access to date without

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:34.961
writing datetime dot date every time Next

00:00:35.224 --> 00:00:37.408
the variable number is assigned the value

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:41.026
eighty-one The program then calculates the square

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:42.895
root by calling math dot square root

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:44.658
and stores the result in a variable

00:00:44.684 --> 00:00:47.803
named root The next line uses random

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.053
dot sample It chooses three values from

00:00:51.066 --> 00:00:53.487
a range of identification numbers between one

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:56.645
thousand and one thousand nine Because this

00:00:56.671 --> 00:00:58.776
is random your result may be different

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:01.303
each time you run the cell The

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:03.289
program then uses date dot today to

00:01:03.316 --> 00:01:05.697
get today's date from the computer environment

00:01:06.618 --> 00:01:09.645
Finally the print statements display four results

00:01:10.566 --> 00:01:12.211
The first should show a square root

00:01:12.237 --> 00:01:15.316
of nine point zero The second displays

00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:17.737
pi rounded to three decimal places which

00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:19.882
should be approximately three point one four

00:01:19.895 --> 00:01:23.500
two The third displays three randomly selected

00:01:23.526 --> 00:01:27.579
identification numbers The final line displays
today's

00:01:27.592 --> 00:01:30.224
date Go ahead and click the Run

00:01:30.237 --> 00:01:33.184
button now If Python is loading for

00:01:33.197 --> 00:01:35.224
the first time wait a few seconds

00:01:36.158 --> 00:01:38.197
Then look at the terminal output below

00:01:38.224 --> 00:01:41.210
the code Pay attention to the random

00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:44.487
sample Run the cell a second time

00:01:45.395 --> 00:01:47.513
The square root and rounded pi should remain

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:50.290
the same but the sample identification numbers

00:01:50.316 --> 00:01:53.776
may change For a small experiment change

00:01:53.803 --> 00:01:55.711
the number from eighty-one to one hundred

00:01:55.737 --> 00:02:00.382
forty-four Run the cell again The square root

00:02:00.408 --> 00:02:03.276
should now be twelve point zero This

00:02:03.303 --> 00:02:07.382
example demonstrates an important idea By importing

00:02:07.408 --> 00:02:10.553
standard-library modules we can use reliable tools

00:02:10.579 --> 00:02:12.908
that already exist instead of writing everything

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:13.553
ourselves
